description:
Read a binary's CodeView record and work out where its PDB lives on a symbol server (lesson 5.04):

```cpp
struct CodeView { std::array<std::uint8_t, 16> guid; std::uint32_t age; std::string path; };

std::optional<CodeView> parseCodeView(const std::vector<std::uint8_t>& record);
std::string pdbName(const std::string& path);
std::string guidText(const std::array<std::uint8_t, 16>& guid);
std::string symbolServerPath(const CodeView& cv);
```

- **parseCodeView** reads the record: `RSDS`, the 16 GUID bytes, a 4-byte little-endian age, then the PDB path up to a zero byte (or the end). Anything shorter than 24 bytes or with another signature gives `std::nullopt`.
- **pdbName** is the file name part of the path: everything after the last `\` or `/`.
- **guidText** formats a GUID the symbol server's way: the first 4 bytes as one little-endian 32-bit number (8 hex digits), the next 2 as a little-endian 16-bit number (4 digits), the next 2 the same, then the last 8 bytes one by one (2 digits each). Uppercase, no separators: 32 characters.
- **symbolServerPath** is `name/GUIDAGE/name`, with the age in uppercase hex without leading zeros.

